      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHIMARI (4) has the most reliable recent profile, with her close Kalgoorlie third two starts back reading well for this and the drop from provincial company giving her a suitable platform to rebound from an even seventh on soft ground. She has placed at the trip and brings the strongest recent figures. PRINCIPAL DEALER (5) has to be forgiven for a plain Mingenew ninth, but her Broome second when beaten half a length gives her a genuine winning case if she can return to that level. INSPIRATIONAL MAC (3) resumes from a long break after provincial maiden runs at Geraldton, and the wide run at his latest appearance gives him some excuse despite the margin. I AM A ROCKSTAR (1) also resumes and changes stable/state; his overall placing record keeps him in the mix, though he has to improve on the two plain runs that ended his last campaign. TEDESCHI (2) won't be far away.",
